                        ],
                        "form": "фарисе́ях"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "435b8a04-e457-31c9-a2d4-1d781e54c718",
                        "entry_id": "009c6333-4962-3eec-b094-a5a3290302a7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "религ., истор., : представитель общественно-религиозного течения, отличавшийся особым догматизмом и ортодоксальностью в исполнении правил благочестия"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "в Иудее во 2 в. до н. э. — 2 в. н. э."
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3d458ff5-1487-4c08-a078-d8eeba7ace8a",
                                "sense_id": "435b8a04-e457-31c9-a2d4-1d781e54c718",
                                "text": "Слово «фарисей» я перевожу православный на том основании, что по всем исследованиям оно значит совершенно то же самое, что значит у нас православный. Слово это происходит от еврейского «параш» и употребляется или в смысле «толкователь» ― за что выдавали себя фарисеи, по Иосифу Флавию, или в смысле «паруш», т. е. тот, который отделяет себя от толпы неверных и считает себя правым, т. е. православным."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "187fea5c-4a3d-3760-8a8a-a33450b395db",
                        "entry_id": "009c6333-4962-3eec-b094-a5a3290302a7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., неодобр. лицемерный человек, ханжа"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d6b2bf1b-319c-4802-8948-f1fac52675c4",
                                "sense_id": "187fea5c-4a3d-3760-8a8a-a33450b395db",
                                "text": "Свинцовою тяжестью всею / Легли на дворы небеса. / Искали улик фарисеи, / Юля перед Ним, как лиса."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6944049e-0cc5-4053-b739-b2cd56378dbe",
                        "source_entry_id": "009c6333-4962-3eec-b094-a5a3290302a7",
                        "source_sense_description": "представитель секты",
                        "target_lang_word": "Pharisee",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Pharisee",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3c34afa4-6f3b-3300-9c8b-8d70bfe1707e",
                                        "entry_id": "cf7e6434-2775-304a-b6e1-932fd37836e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A member of an ancient Jewish political party, a social movement, and a school of thought among Jews that flourished during the Second Temple Era (536 B.C.E.–70 C.E.). The movement was ultimately the basis for most contemporary forms of Judaism."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "001d5ae7-b80e-404e-b8eb-d57ac8300f95",
                                                "sense_id": "3c34afa4-6f3b-3300-9c8b-8d70bfe1707e",
                                                "text": "Then understood they how that he bade them not beware of the leaven of bread, but of the doctrine of the Pharisees and of the Sadducees."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b1d8a06-6594-40d5-8461-448b12508bfd",
                                                "sense_id": "3c34afa4-6f3b-3300-9c8b-8d70bfe1707e",
                                                "text": "I cannot tell. They [Jews]are always doing it. The Pharisees, for instance, say that there are angels, and the Sadducees declare that angels do not exist."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6da67f54-f4ee-3037-b49f-f216d8c98096",
                                        "entry_id": "cf7e6434-2775-304a-b6e1-932fd37836e9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who values the letter of the law over its spirit or intention."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcca898b-9387-498d-9cea-46a42b1ce7b7",
                                                "sense_id": "6da67f54-f4ee-3037-b49f-f216d8c98096",
                                                "text": "He was, and is yet most likely, the wearisomest self-righteous Pharisee that ever ransacked a Bible to rake the promises to himself and fling the curses to his neighbours."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d440e18-4298-471f-b1e0-1db05af1aa51",
                                                "sense_id": "6da67f54-f4ee-3037-b49f-f216d8c98096",
                                                "text": "The spider fattens himself on flies, and the Pharisee has his reward. Foolish persons are easily entrapped by the loud professions of pretenders, and even the more judicious cannot always escape."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8747bb30-0ae4-4ece-bddc-0ced0a63cb93",
                        "source_entry_id": "009c6333-4962-3eec-b094-a5a3290302a7",
                        "source_sense_description": "лицемер",
                        "target_lang_word": "pharisee",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3fe718cf-c67c-4be2-b98c-075cd2f7f976",
                        "source_entry_id": "009c6333-4962-3eec-b094-a5a3290302a7",
                        "source_sense_description": "лицемер",
                        "target_lang_word": "hypocrite",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "hypocrite",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b8ec7efd-76ea-335c-81e4-23065b57ce40",
                                        "entry_id": "0ac6eb15-980d-3fe4-b1b9-843d816ffe95",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who practices hypocrisy, who pretends to hold beliefs, or whose actions are not consistent with their claimed beliefs."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8eeaac0-0d0a-46ce-8432-86a8742bee06",
                                                "sense_id": "b8ec7efd-76ea-335c-81e4-23065b57ce40",
                                                "text": "And when thou prayest, thou shalt not be as the hypocrites are: for they love to pray standing in the synagogues and in the corners of the streets, that they may be seen of men. Verily I say unto you, They have their reward."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ef6bfec-1c91-4796-8f72-dde1e92b94e9",
                                                "sense_id": "b8ec7efd-76ea-335c-81e4-23065b57ce40",
                                                "text": "[S]he was one of your ſoft ſpoken, canting, whining hypocrites, who with a truly jeſuitical art, could wreſt evil out of the moſt inoffenſive thought, word, look or action; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bb069a97-9774-430b-a66e-ebe3f1c121ab",
                                                "sense_id": "b8ec7efd-76ea-335c-81e4-23065b57ce40",
                                                "text": "Neither Mr. Meacham, who mostly ignores Jefferson’s slave ownership, nor Mr. Wiencek, who sees him as a sort of fallen angel who comes to slavery only after discovering how profitable it could be, seem willing to confront the ugly truth: the third president was a creepy, brutal hypocrite."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": [
                    {
